            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107494-libssl3t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107494 medium vulnerability for libssl3t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: The QUIC stack queues a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame also for\nretransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames. This allows a remote malicious\nQUIC stack to queue an unlimited number of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames.\n\nImpact summary: A malicious remote QUIC peer can trigger an out-of-memory\ncondition causing a Denial of Service.\n\nCWE: CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling\n\nDescription: The earlier fix for CVE-2026-84784 was not complete. It\nfailed to ignore retransmissions of the NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame. The QUIC\nimplementation created and inserted a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame for every\nretransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame it received and there was no limit\non how many RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames were queued.\n\nThis issue allows a malicious remote QUIC stack to trigger an unbounded\nallocation of memory and eventually an out-of-memory (OOM) condition.\n\nFIPS impact: no\nThe FIPS module is not affected as the QUIC implementation is outside the\nOpenSSL FIPS module boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107494",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107494\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssl3t64\nVersion: 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-107494](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107494)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107494**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssl3t64  | 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-107494](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107494)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssl3t64@3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107494-openssl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107494 medium vulnerability for openssl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: The QUIC stack queues a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame also for\nretransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames. This allows a remote malicious\nQUIC stack to queue an unlimited number of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames.\n\nImpact summary: A malicious remote QUIC peer can trigger an out-of-memory\ncondition causing a Denial of Service.\n\nCWE: CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling\n\nDescription: The earlier fix for CVE-2026-84784 was not complete. It\nfailed to ignore retransmissions of the NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame. The QUIC\nimplementation created and inserted a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame for every\nretransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame it received and there was no limit\non how many RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames were queued.\n\nThis issue allows a malicious remote QUIC stack to trigger an unbounded\nallocation of memory and eventually an out-of-memory (OOM) condition.\n\nFIPS impact: no\nThe FIPS module is not affected as the QUIC implementation is outside the\nOpenSSL FIPS module boundary."
