            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19445-libpython3.12-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-19445 medium vulnerability for libpython3.12-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A remote, unauthenticated TLS client can make a server crash or call\nthrough a freed pointer if its sni_callback assigns a different context to\nSSLSocket.context (the documented way to select a certificate per server\nname) and nothing else keeps the original ssl.SSLContext alive. Typical\ncases are servers that create an SSLContext per connection or replace it\nwhile connections are open; servers that wrap their listening socket with\nit are not affected.\n\n\nMitigation: keep a reference to every SSLContext that sets sni_callback for\nthe lifetime of the server. TLS clients are not affected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19445",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19445\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.12-minimal\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.17\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-19445](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19445)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-19445**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libpython3.12-minimal  | 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.17  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-19445](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19445)  |\n"
              },
