            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-133949-python3-pip-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-133949 medium vulnerability for python3-pip-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "pip prior to v26.2.2 the certifi bundled with pip contains the compromised eMudhra certificates. \n\n\n\n\nUpgrading to a secure version of pip should be done either by first upgrading Python to a version that rejects the compromised intermediates (CVE-2026-115557) or use hash pinning with a known-secure version of pip. pip is not vulnerable when using a Python version that rejects the compromised certificates. See the references below for more information."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-133949",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-133949\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3-pip-whl\nVersion: 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-133949](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-133949)",
