            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-121482-libssl3t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-121482 medium vulnerability for libssl3t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: Verifying a maliciously crafted CMS or PKCS#7 SignedData\nmessage with CRL checking enabled may consume excessive CPU time, growing with\nthe square of the message size.\n\nImpact summary: An attacker who can submit a CMS or PKCS#7 SignedData message\nto an application that verifies it with CRL checking enabled can occupy a CPU\ncore for seconds to minutes, causing Denial of Service. Applications that\nleave CRL checking disabled are not affected.\n\nCWE: CWE-407: Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity\n\nDescription: With CRL checking enabled, OpenSSL compares each CRL distribution\npoint of a certificate against the issuing distribution point of every\ncandidate CRL. For a nameRelativeToCRLIssuer distribution point, the full name\nis the CRL issuer name with the relative name appended. Since the change that\ndeferred this computation, crl_crldp_check() rebuilds that full name for each\ncandidate CRL and frees it again.\n\nCMS_verify() and PKCS7_verify() take both the distribution points and the\ncandidate CRLs from the message, and this scoring runs before any signature is\nchecked. An application is exposed only if it sets X509_V_FLAG_CRL_CHECK on\nthe store and does not pass CMS_NOCRL or PKCS7_NOCRL; CRL checking is off by\ndefault. In TLS the CRLs come from the local store, so a peer controls only\nthe distribution point count.\n\nThe cost grows with the product of the distribution point count, the CRL count\nand the issuer name length, all chosen by the message author; a few hundred\nkilobytes can occupy a CPU core for tens of seconds. Verification still fails\nas it should, with no crash, no incorrect result and no memory growth.\nRequiring CRL checking is what limits the severity.\n\nFIPS impact: no\nThe affected code is outside the FIPS module boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-121482",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-121482\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssl3t64\nVersion: 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-121482](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-121482)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-121482**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssl3t64  | 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-121482](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-121482)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssl3t64@3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-84786-libssl3t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-84786 medium vulnerability for libssl3t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: A DANE-enabled TLS client may crash by dereferencing a NULL\npointer when processing an unusual combination of certificate and TLSA\nrecords.\n\nImpact summary: The impact is limited to a client crash (potential Denial\nof Service).\n\nCWE: CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference\n\nDescription: A DANE-enabled TLS client that supports TLSA records with at\nleast one of the PKIX-TA(0) or PKIX-EE(1) usages alongside the DANE-TA(2)\nusage may crash by dereferencing a NULL pointer if the server claims a trusted\nCA's certificate to be its end-entity certificate and has an unusual mix of\nassociated TLSA records.\n\nDANE SMTP clients should not be affected since only the\nDANE-TA(2) and DANE-EE(3) TLSA record usages are specified applicable\nin SMTP.  For example, the Postfix MTA is not affected, while the Exim\nMTA does not at present use OpenSSL's DANE implementation.\n\nUse of DANE in validation of RFC7250 raw public keys (RPKs) is also\nunaffected, as these only use DANE-EE(3) TLSA records.\n\nOnly applications that support combining the DANE PKI with a traditional PKI\nare potentially affected.  A DANE-enabled browser or similar, that uses\nOpenSSL's DANE API could be affected.\n\nFIPS impact: no\nThe DANE API is outside the FIPS module boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-84786",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-84786\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssl3t64\nVersion: 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-84786](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-84786)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-84786**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssl3t64  | 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-84786](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-84786)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssl3t64@3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
