            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97689-python3-pip-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97689 medium vulnerability for python3-pip-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "urllib3 is an HTTP client library for Python. From 1.10.3 until 2.8.0, the HTTPResponse.read_chunked and HTTPResponse.stream methods can allocate unbounded memory because the streaming chunk parser buffers the chunk-size field until newline or EOF without a length bound. The trigger is that a malicious server returns Transfer-Encoding: chunked followed by a very long run of bytes without a newline. The attack mechanism is that a malicious HTTP server sends a very long unterminated chunk-size line. The impact is that unbounded memory allocation can exhaust the client process. This issue is fixed in version 2.8.0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-97689",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97689\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3-pip-whl\nVersion: 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-97689](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-97689)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97689**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3-pip-whl  | 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-97689](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-97689)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/python3-pip-whl@24.0%2Bdfsg-1ubuntu1.3?arch=all\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=python-pip"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-100290-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-100290 medium vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The regcomp and regexec functions in the GNU C Library version 2.3 to version 2.44 may read freed memory and free the same heap block twice when a memory allocation fails while a regular expression is compiled or matched.  The re_dfa_add_node (the NFA node table) and build_range_exp (bracket ranges) grow several arrays with consecutive realloc calls and store the new pointers only after all of them succeed.  When a later call fails, the pattern buffer keeps pointers to blocks that were already freed, and the error cleanup frees them again.  In regexec, the back-reference cache (match_ctx_add_entry) frees its array when a realloc fails but keeps the pointer, which is freed again on the error path.\n\nAn attacker does not need to supply a crafted regular expression: patterns large enough to grow these arrays are common.  The failure has to hit a specific allocation, though, so the issue can only be reached when the system is already under memory pressure.  An attacker who supplies the pattern or the subject string has little control over which allocation fails, so the expected impact is a crash of the process.  This issue affects all architectures and ABIs supported by the GNU C Library."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-100290",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-100290\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.39-0ubuntu8.12\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libc-bin.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-100290](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-100290)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-100290**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libc-bin  | 2.39-0ubuntu8.12  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libc-bin.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-100290](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-100290)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libc-bin@2.39-0ubuntu8.12?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.7"
              }
            },
