              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13346-python3-pip-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13346 medium vulnerability for python3-pip-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "pip would incorrectly handle doubly-encoded package URLs from indexes allowing for files to be installed to arbitrary locations on disk even when installing wheels.\n\n\n\n\nThis vulnerability requires downloading or installing a package from a malicious package index to succeed, malicious packages alone are not able to exploit this vulnerability. Note that this vulnerability only materially impacts users running `pip download` with the `--only-binary` option as installing source distributions from an untrusted index is already an unsafe operation that executes code during install time."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13346",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13346\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3-pip-whl\nVersion: 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-13346](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13346)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-13346**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3-pip-whl  | 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-13346](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13346)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/python3-pip-whl@24.0%2Bdfsg-1ubuntu1.3?arch=all\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=python-pip"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-121758-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-121758 medium vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Converting crafted ISO-2022-CN-EXT input in the GNU C Library version 2.2 through 2.44 may result in the converter reading past the end of the input buffer, causing the calling application to crash.\n\nWhen the ISO-2022-CN-EXT decoder encounters an invalid input byte sequence like '\\x0e' it ends up advancing the pointer tracking the read buffer position twice.  If this sequence is at the end of the input buffer, the decoder may then end up reading past the bounds of the input buffer.  To exploit this, the input and encoding needs to be attacker controlled."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-121758",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-121758\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.39-0ubuntu8.12\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libc-bin.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-121758](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-121758)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-121758**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libc-bin  | 2.39-0ubuntu8.12  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libc-bin.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-121758](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-121758)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libc-bin@2.39-0ubuntu8.12?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
