            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59890-python3-setuptools-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59890 medium vulnerability for python3-setuptools-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "setuptools is a package that allows users to download, build, install, upgrade, and uninstall Python packages. Prior to 83.0.0, FileList applied MANIFEST.in exclude, global-exclude, recursive-exclude, and prune directives by matching compiled glob patterns against on-disk file names without Unicode normalization, so on macOS APFS or HFS+ an NFD file name could bypass an NFC exclusion rule and be packed into a source distribution. This issue is fixed in version 83.0.0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59890",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59890\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3-setuptools-whl\nVersion: 68.1.2-2ubuntu1.2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-setuptools-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-59890](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59890)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59890**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3-setuptools-whl  | 68.1.2-2ubuntu1.2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-setuptools-whl.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-59890](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59890)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/python3-setuptools-whl@68.1.2-2ubuntu1.2?arch=all\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=setuptools"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107496-libssl3t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107496 medium vulnerability for libssl3t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: Encrypting a CMS message to an EC certificate whose group order\nis 1 may cause CMS_encrypt() or CMS_encrypt_ex() to loop indefinitely.\n\nImpact summary: An attacker able to supply the recipient certificate to an\napplication performing CMS encryption can cause that application to loop\nindefinitely, consuming CPU and resulting in Denial of Service.\n\nCWE: CWE-835: Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop')\n\nDescription: CMS_encrypt() and CMS_encrypt_ex() encrypt a message to one or\nmore recipient certificates and, for an EC recipient, generate an ephemeral\nkey in the recipient's group. If the certificate declares a group order of 1,\nrandom scalar generation can only produce zero. The key generation routine\nthen retries without limit while waiting for a nonzero private scalar, so the\ncall never returns.\n\nThe OpenSSL TLS and QUIC implementations do not use this path. An application\nis exposed only if it calls CMS_encrypt() or CMS_encrypt_ex() with a recipient\ncertificate whose EC parameters are attacker-controlled. Certificates with\nnormal EC group orders do not trigger the loop.\n\nOpenSSL 4.0 and later reject unknown explicit EC groups in default builds.\nThese versions are affected only when configured with the\nenable-ec_explicit_curves option.\n\nThe result is a hang that consumes a CPU core until the process is\ninterrupted, a Denial of Service. The severity is Low because the attacker\nmust supply the recipient certificate and the application must choose to\nencrypt to it; ordinary CMS encryption to trusted recipients is unaffected.\n\nThe fix makes EC key generation fail when the group has no valid nonzero\nprivate scalar, instead of retrying indefinitely.\n\nFIPS impact: no\nThe FIPS modules in 4.1, 4.0, 3.5 and 3.0 are not affected. The FIPS provider\ndoes not support arbitrary explicit EC domain parameters, so an order-1 group\nis rejected during key import before the vulnerable key generation path is\nreached."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107496",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107496\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssl3t64\nVersion: 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-107496](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107496)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107496**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssl3t64  | 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-107496](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107496)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssl3t64@3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107496-openssl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107496 medium vulnerability for openssl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: Encrypting a CMS message to an EC certificate whose group order\nis 1 may cause CMS_encrypt() or CMS_encrypt_ex() to loop indefinitely.\n\nImpact summary: An attacker able to supply the recipient certificate to an\napplication performing CMS encryption can cause that application to loop\nindefinitely, consuming CPU and resulting in Denial of Service.\n\nCWE: CWE-835: Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop')\n\nDescription: CMS_encrypt() and CMS_encrypt_ex() encrypt a message to one or\nmore recipient certificates and, for an EC recipient, generate an ephemeral\nkey in the recipient's group. If the certificate declares a group order of 1,\nrandom scalar generation can only produce zero. The key generation routine\nthen retries without limit while waiting for a nonzero private scalar, so the\ncall never returns.\n\nThe OpenSSL TLS and QUIC implementations do not use this path. An application\nis exposed only if it calls CMS_encrypt() or CMS_encrypt_ex() with a recipient\ncertificate whose EC parameters are attacker-controlled. Certificates with\nnormal EC group orders do not trigger the loop.\n\nOpenSSL 4.0 and later reject unknown explicit EC groups in default builds.\nThese versions are affected only when configured with the\nenable-ec_explicit_curves option.\n\nThe result is a hang that consumes a CPU core until the process is\ninterrupted, a Denial of Service. The severity is Low because the attacker\nmust supply the recipient certificate and the application must choose to\nencrypt to it; ordinary CMS encryption to trusted recipients is unaffected.\n\nThe fix makes EC key generation fail when the group has no valid nonzero\nprivate scalar, instead of retrying indefinitely.\n\nFIPS impact: no\nThe FIPS modules in 4.1, 4.0, 3.5 and 3.0 are not affected. The FIPS provider\ndoes not support arbitrary explicit EC domain parameters, so an order-1 group\nis rejected during key import before the vulnerable key generation path is\nreached."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107496",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107496\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: openssl\nVersion: 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/openssl.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-107496](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107496)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107496**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | openssl  | 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/openssl.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-107496](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-107496)  |\n"
