            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-127231-libgnutls30t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-127231 medium vulnerability for libgnutls30t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A double free in the X.509 name constraints enforcement of GnuTLS 3.8.13 on all platforms allows a remote attacker to cause a denial of service (application crash) via a certificate chain containing a NameConstraints extension processed while the application is under memory pressure. When an already populated name constraints object is reinitialized, previously freed list pointers are not cleared, so a memory allocation failure precisely at reinitialization leaves a dangling pointer that is freed again during a later cleanup."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-127231",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-127231\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libgnutls30t64\nVersion: 3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.6\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libgnutls30t64:amd64.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-127231](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-127231)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-127231**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libgnutls30t64  | 3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.6  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libgnutls30t64:amd64.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-127231](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-127231)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libgnutls30t64@3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.6?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=gnutls28"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-115819-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-115819 medium vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling the wide scanf family of functions (swscanf, fwscanf, wscanf, vswscanf, vfwscanf and vwscanf) with a %s or %[ conversion without the 'l' length modifier in the GNU C Library version 2.2 to version 2.44 writes an extra null byte one past the end of the destination array when the converted multibyte string and its terminating null byte exactly fill that array.\n\nThese conversions store each wide input character into the caller's char array as a multibyte sequence.  The conversion ends with the sequence that returns to the initial shift state, which also stores the terminating null byte, and the functions then append a second null byte.  A destination sized for the converted string and one terminator, as the C standard requires the caller to provide, is therefore written one byte past its end.  The out-of-bounds byte is always a null byte, which may corrupt adjacent data or crash the process.  An attacker who supplies the input can trigger the overflow with a string whose converted length exactly fills the destination.\n\nThe narrow scanf functions, the %ls and %l[ conversions into a wchar_t array, and the 'a' and 'm' allocation modifiers are not affected, and storing a wide scanf conversion into a narrow char array is uncommon.  This issue affects all architectures and ABIs supported by the GNU C Library."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-115819",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-115819\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.39-0ubuntu8.12\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libc-bin.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-115819](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-115819)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-115819**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libc-bin  | 2.39-0ubuntu8.12  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libc-bin.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-115819](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-115819)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libc-bin@2.39-0ubuntu8.12?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8"
              }
            },
