            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97687-python3-pip-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97687 medium vulnerability for python3-pip-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "urllib3 is an HTTP client library for Python. From 1.26.0 until 2.8.0, the proxy_ssl_context, proxy_assert_hostname, proxy_assert_fingerprint, ssl_context, cert_reqs, verify_mode, use_forwarding_for_https=True, and CERT_NONE configuration paths fail to remain separated because target-server TLS settings are incorrectly applied to the HTTPS proxy connection. The trigger is that an application uses an HTTPS proxy and configures target-server TLS settings that must remain separate from the proxy TLS handshake, including HTTPS forwarding with target-specific identity or credentials. Applying cert_reqs=CERT_NONE can overwrite proxy_ssl_context.verify_mode in place, and the mutation persists so later connections reusing the same context may connect to the HTTPS proxy without certificate verification. The attack mechanism is that an attacker intercepts and impersonates the HTTPS proxy after the effective proxy policy accepts the attacker's certificate. The impact is that the attacker can observe or modify forwarded traffic or receive a target TLS client certificate, while CONNECT tunneling still preserves the separate end-to-end target TLS connection. This issue is fixed in version 2.8.0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-97687",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97687\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3-pip-whl\nVersion: 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-97687](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-97687)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97687**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3-pip-whl  | 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-97687](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-97687)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/python3-pip-whl@24.0%2Bdfsg-1ubuntu1.3?arch=all\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=python-pip"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-95691-libssl3t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-95691 medium vulnerability for libssl3t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: A retransmitted QUIC CRYPTO frame can release packet storage\nwhile the TLS record layer retains a direct pointer into that storage causing\nuse after free.\n\nImpact summary: A malicious QUIC server can cause a heap-use-after-free read\nin the OpenSSL QUIC client. The server can also identify one allocator-adjacent\nbyte through the client's protected Handshake response.\n\nCWE: CWE-416: Use After Free\n\nDescription: During CRYPTO stream processing, a pointer into the first frame's\nmemory on the stream is lent to the TLS handshake processing. The memory\nmust remain stable until it is processed and released. However the processing\nof retransmitted CRYPTO frames could release the memory if the retransmitted\nframe fully overlapped the existing frame. This then causes use-after-free read\nwhen the TLS handshake processing continues.\n\nThe use-after-free read can lead to a Denial-of-Service of the client\napplication or a minor leak of information about the heap memory contents\nthat might be overwritten with other data, subsequently allocated by\nthe application, to the peer.\n\nFIPS impact: no\nThe FIPS module is not affected as the QUIC implementation is outside of\nthe OpenSSL FIPS module boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-95691",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-95691\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssl3t64\nVersion: 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-95691](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-95691)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-95691**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssl3t64  | 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libssl3t64:amd64.md5sums  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-95691](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-95691)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssl3t64@3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-95691-openssl",
