            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-102474-dash",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-102474 medium vulnerability for dash package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in dash. The printf builtin reserves four bytes before converting a Unicode \\u or \\U escape, but the multi-byte token can need five or six bytes. A local user who can supply such an escape to dash printf or echo %b, including through dash -c and a positional argument, can write one or two bytes past that reservation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-102474",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-102474\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: dash\nVersion: 0.5.12-6ubuntu5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/dash.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-102474](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-102474)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-102474**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | dash  | 0.5.12-6ubuntu5  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/dash.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-102474](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-102474)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/dash@0.5.12-6ubuntu5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-118444-libpython3.12-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-118444 medium vulnerability for libpython3.12-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Out-of-bounds read vulnerabilities in the pybddisasm Python bindings may disclose adjacent process memory during instruction decoding. The nd_decode function may read up to 15 bytes without checking the actual length of the supplied Python buffer. The nd_decode_ex, nd_decode_ex2, and nd_decode_with_context functions pass the caller-supplied buffer size to the decoder without validating it against the actual length of the Python buffer. Data read beyond the buffer may be exposed through nd_get_instrux_bytes, which returns a fixed-length list of 16 bytes. Exploitation requires an application to invoke the affected APIs with a short buffer or an oversized length and to expose the resulting bytes to an attacker. The pybddisasm package is no longer maintained."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-118444",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-118444\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.12-minimal\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.17\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-118444](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-118444)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-118444**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libpython3.12-minimal  | 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.17  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-118444](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-118444)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libpython3.12-minimal@3.12.3-1ubuntu0.17?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=python3.12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-118447-libpython3.12-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-118447 medium vulnerability for libpython3.12-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use of uninitialized memory vulnerability in the pybddisasm Python bindings may disclose process memory when instruction decoding fails. The nd_decode, nd_decode_ex, nd_decode_ex2, and nd_decode_with_context functions may return an INSTRUX object whose contents have not been initialized after an unsuccessful decoding operation, including failures caused by invalid parameters. Accessing members of the returned object may expose residual process memory. Exploitation requires an application to access and expose the returned object contents after a decoding failure. The pybddisasm package is no longer maintained."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-118447",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-118447\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.12-minimal\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.17\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-118447](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-118447)",
