            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-118448-libpython3.12-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-118448 medium vulnerability for libpython3.12-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use of uninitialized memory vulnerability in the pybddisasm Python bindings affects nd_to_text. If the underlying text conversion fails, including failures caused by invalid parameters, the output buffer may remain uninitialized while still being converted into a Python return value. This may disclose residual process memory or cause the Python process to crash. Exploitation requires an application to invoke nd_to_text in a way that causes conversion to fail and to return or otherwise use the resulting output. The pybddisasm package is no longer maintained."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-118448",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-118448\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.12-minimal\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.17\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-118448](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-118448)",
