            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25645-python3-pip-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-25645 low vulnerability for python3-pip-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Requests is a HTTP library. Prior to version 2.33.0, the `requests.utils.extract_zipped_paths()` utility function uses a predictable filename when extracting files from zip archives into the system temporary directory. If the target file already exists, it is reused without validation. A local attacker with write access to the temp directory could pre-create a malicious file that would be loaded in place of the legitimate one. Standard usage of the Requests library is not affected by this vulnerability. Only applications that call `extract_zipped_paths()` directly are impacted. Starting in version 2.33.0, the library extracts files to a non-deterministic location. If developers are unable to upgrade, they can set `TMPDIR` in their environment to a directory with restricted write access."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-25645",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-25645\nSeverity: low\nPackage: python3-pip-whl\nVersion: 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-25645](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-25645)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-25645**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | python3-pip-whl  | 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-25645](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-25645)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/python3-pip-whl@24.0%2Bdfsg-1ubuntu1.3?arch=all\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=python-pip"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54370-libacl1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-54370 medium vulnerability for libacl1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "acl before version 2.4.0 contains a time-of-check to time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition vulnerability that allows local attackers to escalate privileges by replacing a pathname component with a symbolic link between an lstat() check and subsequent symlink-following operations such as stat(), chown(), chmod(), acl_get_file(), and acl_set_file(). Attackers who control a pathname component can redirect file access control list operations to arbitrary files when getfacl, setfacl, or chacl is invoked by a privileged process over an attacker-controlled path, resulting in local privilege escalation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54370\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libacl1\nVersion: 2.3.2-1build1.1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libacl1:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-54370](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54370**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libacl1  | 2.3.2-1build1.1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libacl1:amd64.md5sums  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-54370](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libacl1@2.3.2-1build1.1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=acl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.2"
              }
